        "id": 1511343
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-04-01T12:24:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The problem is that I want to clear actions in `usb_malfunction_sink_after`, so if it was local variable it would be out of the scope. Zephyr FIFO expects that structure that is put has `void*` field reserved for internal FIFO usage, so it is not allocating anything on `k_fifo_put`.\n\nI agree that actions in the fixture is strange. What do you think about making static variable in the test instead?",
      "parentUuid": "162ffde9_cbb3cb5e",
      "revId": "5581b93187c4d24978d7f73318e4783b9898d4ae",
